      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-general-1-2003-p4.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "84\n\nAn integer has an odd number of divisors precisely if it is a square. So we take the 90 2 -digit numbers \\((10,11, \\ldots, 99)\\) and remove the 6 squares \\(\\left(4^{2}, 5^{2}, \\ldots, 9^{2}\\right)\\), for a total of 84.",
